{
 "brief": "The White House does not appear concerned by Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's rejection of a peace plan for Gaza, according to Axios, viewing his stance as part of his political calculations. The Trump administration's muted response suggests confidence that Netanyahu's public resistance reflects domestic political positioning rather than a fundamental obstacle to negotiations.\n\nNetanyahu has previously rejected peace proposals amid pressure from far-right coalition partners opposed to ending the Gaza conflict. The divergence between Washington and Jerusalem over the plan's fate reflects the gap between the Trump administration's diplomatic agenda and the Israeli government's stated position on the region.",
